RANGE:	                           CIDR:             SIZE:              TYPICAL USE:
10.0.0.0    –  10.255.255.255	   10.0.0.0/8	      ~16.7M addresses   	Large networks, cloud, corporate
172.16.0.0  –  172.31.255.255	   172.16.0.0/12	  ~1M addresses	      Mid-size; Docker uses this by default
192.168.0.0 –  192.168.255.255	 192.168.0.0/16	  ~65k addresses	    Home/small networks (most routers)

RFC1918: Anything in them is yours to assign; they never route on the public internet.
169.254.x.x — link-local (APIPA). A device gives itself one of these when it fails to get an IP from DHCP. Seeing it = "no DHCP." Never assign it manually.
127.0.0.1 — localhost, this machine only. Not for other devices.
Reserve .1 — it's almost always the router/gateway.
Broadcast: .255 (the top of a /24) is the broadcast address — not assignable to a device.


